From 3e2ba647072101631e4da68a2cce87fb8d87c978 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ifran Ali <khanu.i.i.k.2000@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 03:31:54 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] optical: airoha: accept 0xa0-byte vendor BOB images

EcoNet/TP-Link firmware stores the LDD/LA BOB as 0xa0 bytes: the words
up to and including the PON magic at 0x94. The TP-Link XZ000-G3 keeps
it at factoryinfo+0x16 and places an unrelated 40-byte ASCII ID
directly after it, so an NVMEM cell cannot be widened to 161 bytes
without feeding that ID into the LUT words at 0xa0.

Words past the imported length already read back as erased, so lower
the minimum to 0xa0.

Signed-off-by: Ifran Ali <khanu.i.i.k.2000@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/net/optical/airoha/airoha_lddla.h | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/optical/airoha/airoha_lddla.h b/drivers/net/optical/airoha/airoha_lddla.h
index bc6428689..d8fd5ec3c 100644
--- a/drivers/net/optical/airoha/airoha_lddla.h
+++ b/drivers/net/optical/airoha/airoha_lddla.h
@@ -42,7 +42,8 @@ struct airoha_lddla;
 #define AIROHA_LDDLA_FLASH_ERASED	0xffffffff
 #define AIROHA_LDDLA_BOB_MAGIC_OFFSET		0x094
 #define AIROHA_LDDLA_BOB_MAX_SIZE		512
-#define AIROHA_LDDLA_BOB_MIN_SIZE		161
+/* Vendor flash stores only the words up to the magic; the rest reads erased */
+#define AIROHA_LDDLA_BOB_MIN_SIZE		0xa0
 
 /*
  * Every known Airoha LDD/LA BOB magic has the form 0xPP0507CC:
-- 
2.43.0

